From 2b83685977256ec983346752904eaf61657e38ec Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FiyeroT <me@fiyero.xyz>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 23:26:55 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 70/71] listener: the connections an inbound still holds end
 with it

A TCP connection a listener accepted is ended by what the router dialed for it, or by its peer. One
whose inbound still holds it has nothing dialed: a client of an HTTP proxy between two requests of a
connection kept alive, a handshake that does not come. Such a connection stayed open when the box
closed, and was served on by its closed inbound: the next request of the kept-alive connection was
authenticated by the users the inbound had, and answered "502 Bad Gateway" by the closed router.

The listener keeps the connections whose handler has not returned and closes them when it is closed.
A handler returns when the connection is closed or when the router has it: a connection that was
handed over is not touched. The client sees its connection closed, as by any HTTP server that stops,
and dials again.

The module is a file of its own; the hooks are a field and the close in listener.go and the call of
the handler in listener_tcp.go.

Measured with podkop-exp (lab/runs/2026-11-22-mixedkeep): the kept-alive connection answered 502 once
after a restart. Tests: TestCloseEndsHeldConnections, TestHeldConnectionsForgotten (the listener),
TestKeptAliveConnectionEndsWithBox (a box with a mixed inbound).

A patch of its own (0801).

Pdk-Feature: listener-held
Pdk-Zone: core
Pdk-Layer: 08
